// SnakeGame.performMove(), last line
scoringRule.onMove();

onMove() is called at the very END of performMove(), after any food has been scored. Why does that ordering matter for a power-up lasting exactly one move?,It does not matter - the count would be the same either way,"If it ticked first, a one-move power-up would drop to zero before the food eaten on that same move was scored, so the effect the player just activated would never apply",Ticking first would double-count the move,Ticking last means the power-up lasts one move longer than requested,,2,Off-by-one bugs in timed effects almost always come down to whether the clock advances before or after the thing being timed.,2

