// SnakeGame
public Point getHead() { return body.peekFirst(); }

getHead() returns the Point object straight out of the body. Given how Point is written elsewhere in the project, is that a leak like TransactionManager returning its live list?,Yes - the caller could move the snake's head by changing the returned Point,"No. Point's row and col are final with no setters, so the returned object cannot be altered - handing out a reference to an immutable value is safe in a way that handing out a mutable list is not",Yes - any object returned from a getter can be modified,"No, because peekFirst() returns a copy",,2,"The useful contrast with the vending machine's leaked list: what makes returning internals dangerous is mutability, not the act of returning them. Immutable values can be shared freely.",2
